From 15de4d8c4cdd40d0c3fbfcb4eb9cdb581498d86f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:32:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0043-vela-vk-defer hooks: the existing inline Vulkan hooks
 (VulkanwDx12_Hooks.cpp: vkBeginCommandBuffer, vkResetCommandBuffer,
 vkAllocate/FreeCommandBuffers, command pool create/reset/destroy,
 vkCmdBeginRenderPass/2/2KHR, vkCmdBeginRendering/KHR and their ends,
 vkCmdExecuteCommands, vkQueueSubmit/2/2KHR) feed hooks/VelaVkDefer: a
 deferred upscale is recorded into a primary command buffer of our own (own
 pool on the family of the game's pool, else the first graphics+compute
 family; 4 buffers with fences) and submitted on the game's queue from inside
 the vkQueueSubmit* hook, after the game's submit returned, same thread; jobs
 no hook submitted go out at the start of the next Evaluate (fallback path,
 queue 0 of the family). Game inputs go assumed layout -> SHADER_READ_ONLY ->
 back around the feature (one table kGameLayoutDefaults: colour 2, depth 3,
 motion 2, output 1; VELA_VK_DEFER_LAYOUTS=c,d,m,o), a new output image is
 cleared once ahead of the game's buffers (VELA_VK_DEFER_CLEAR=0 = no), a job
 older than 1 s is dropped. Nothing calls Enable() yet: the hooks are no-ops

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
